			<div class="section-title" style="padding-top: 12px;"><span class="icon icon-tool"></span> AI Tools <span style="font-weight: normal; opacity: 0.65;">(experimental)</span></div>
			<small style="display: block; padding-bottom: 4px;">Lets the AI chat look up your deal and log data by calling read-only tools, instead of the Deal Context router guessing what to include. Needs a provider/model that supports tool-calling (a recent Llama/Qwen on Ollama, or OpenAI); if unsupported it falls back automatically. Tool use is most reliable on a capable model (llama3.1:8b or qwen2.5:7b/14b and up); on limited hardware you can run a smaller, faster model with AI Tools off and rely on the Deal Context router instead. Read-only &mdash; it can look up deals and logs, never change them.<br><b>You don&rsquo;t need to change any of the options below to get accurate answers</b> &mdash; the defaults are the recommended balance of accuracy and speed. Each toggle only adds extra depth in exchange for a little more time; turn one on only if you want that specific behavior.</small>

			<table id="botsCreate" style="margin-top: 5px;" cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2" style="padding-bottom:4px;">
					<a href="#" id="aiAdvToggle" style="font-size: var(--fs-body); opacity:0.8; text-decoration:none;" onclick="var rows=document.querySelectorAll('.ai-adv-row'); var showing=this.getAttribute('data-on')==='1'; for(var i=0;i&lt;rows.length;i++){rows[i].style.display=showing?'none':'table-row';} this.setAttribute('data-on', showing?'0':'1'); this.textContent=(showing?'\u2699 Show advanced options':'\u2699 Hide advanced options'); return false;">&#9881; Show advanced options</a>
				</td>
			</tr>

			<tr class="ai-adv-row" style="display:none;">
				<td>
					<label for="ai_tools_max_iterations">Max Tool Rounds:
						<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
							<b>Leave at 5 (the default) unless you have a reason to change it.</b> This is how many tool-call rounds the model may take before it must answer (1&ndash;10). Higher allows more lookups on a complex question but is slower; lower is faster but may cut a multi-step answer short.
						</span></span>
					</label>
				</td>
				<td style="width: 325px;">
					<input type="number" id="ai_tools_max_iterations" name="ai_tools_max_iterations" class="form-field" min="1" max="10" style="width:80px;" value="<%= (((services['ai']||{})['tools'])||{})['max_iterations'] || 5 %>">
				</td>
			</tr>


			<tr class="ai-adv-row" style="display:none;">
				<td>
					<label for="toggleAiToolsVerify">Verify answers:
						<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
							<b>Recommended: off &mdash; answers are already checked against your data.</b> With this on, an extra pass double-checks the figures a second time and adds a small &ldquo;please verify&rdquo; note if anything looks unsupported. It does not make answers more accurate; it only adds an extra caution, at the cost of one more model call (slower) per answer. Turn it on only if you want that belt-and-braces check.
						</span></span>
					</label>
				</td>
				<td>
					<input type="checkbox" id="toggleAiToolsVerify" name="ai_tools_verify" class="form-field">
				</td>
			</tr>

			<tr class="ai-adv-row" style="display:none;">
				<td>
					<label for="toggleAiToolsExplore">Deep research (explore):
						<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
							<b>Advanced &mdash; most users leave this off.</b> Adds an <b>explore</b> tool the chat can use for broad, multi-step questions &mdash; it hands the question to a focused sub-agent that gathers and compares a lot of data across many deals/pairs/logs on its own, then returns one synthesized answer, keeping the main chat tidy. More capable but more expensive (a nested loop of model calls, bounded by Max Tool Rounds and a time limit); best on a capable model. Requires AI Tools on. Off by default. Read-only.
						</span></span>
					</label>
				</td>
				<td>
					<input type="checkbox" id="toggleAiToolsExplore" name="ai_tools_explore" class="form-field">
				</td>
			</tr>

				<tr class="ai-adv-row" style="display:none;">
					<td>
						<label for="toggleAiToolsDeepExplore">Deep analysis:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								<b>Advanced &mdash; an add-on to Deep research; most users leave this off.</b> Makes <b>explore</b> work in structured steps &mdash; it breaks a hard question into sub-questions, investigates each, checks for anything still missing, then writes one answer that cites the figures it found. More thorough for questions like &ldquo;why did my portfolio underperform this week across bots?&rdquo;, at the cost of a few extra model calls. It automatically falls back to the single-pass explore when the model can&rsquo;t sustain the extra structure. Requires Deep research (explore) on. Off by default. Read-only.
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>
					<td>
						<input type="checkbox" id="toggleAiToolsDeepExplore" name="ai_tools_deep_explore" class="form-field">
					</td>
				</tr>

			<tr>
				<td>Enabled:</td>
				<td>
					<input type="checkbox" id="toggleAiTools" name="ai_tools_enabled" class="form-field">
				</td>
			</tr>

			</table>

						<div class="section-title" style="padding-top: 12px;"><span class="icon icon-brain"></span> AI Learning <span style="font-weight: normal; opacity: 0.65;">(experimental)</span></div>
			<small style="display: block; padding-bottom: 4px;">When on, the chat remembers which read-only tools answered past questions &mdash; <b>patterns only, never your values</b> (no P/L, balances, prices or deal ids) &mdash; and reuses similar past ones so answers get more accurate over time. Off by default; needs <b>AI Tools</b> on. The learned corpus is kept out of System Backups, and can be <b>exported / imported</b> as a validated pack to seed a new install or share between instances (a Hub that shares one database aggregates its instances automatically).</small>

			<table id="botsCreate" style="margin-top: 5px;" cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0>

			<tr>
				<td>
					<label>Patterns learned:
						<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
							How many question&rarr;tool patterns are stored, and where they came from: <b>local</b> (learned here), <b>seed</b> (shipped with SymBot), <b>community</b> (imported), or <b>hub</b> (aggregated).
						</span></span>
					</label>
				</td>
				<td><span id="ai_learning_stats" style="opacity: 0.75;">&mdash;</span></td>
			</tr>

			<tr>
				<td>
					<label>Corpus pack:
						<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
							<b>Export</b> downloads a validated, patterns-only pack (no values). <b>Import</b> merges a pack from another install &mdash; it is verified (format + integrity checksum + every tool must exist here) before anything is added, so an invalid or tampered file is rejected.
						</span></span>
					</label>
				</td>
				<td>
					<button type="button" id="btnLearningExport" class="btnAll">Export</button>
					<input type="file" id="learningImportFile" accept="application/json,.json" style="display:none;">
					<button type="button" id="btnLearningImport" class="btnAll">Import</button>
					<span id="ai_learning_import_msg" style="opacity: 0.8; margin-left: 6px;"></span>
				</td>
			</tr>

			<tr>
				<td>
					<label>Aggregate &amp; verify:
						<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
							Combine question&rarr;tool patterns other people have shared with you, and &mdash; before saving anything &mdash; see whether it actually helps. SymBot answers a built-in set of practice questions with and without the new patterns and shows whether it now points to the right tool more often (overall and per tool). Patterns many people learned independently are trusted; where people disagree on the same question it is flagged rather than guessed, and one-off patterns are left out. Nothing is saved until you click Adopt.
						</span></span>
					</label>
				</td>
				<td>
					<input type="file" id="learningAggFiles" accept="application/json,.json" multiple style="display:none;">
					<button type="button" id="btnLearningAggregate" class="btnAll">Aggregate &amp; verify&hellip;</button>
					<button type="button" id="btnLearningEvaluate" class="btnAll">Check current accuracy</button>
					<div id="ai_learning_agg_report" style="margin-top:8px; font-size:0.92rem; line-height:1.5; display:none;"></div>
				</td>
			</tr>

			<tr>
				<td>Enabled:</td>
				<td>
					<input type="checkbox" id="toggleAiLearning" name="ai_learning_enabled" class="form-field">
				</td>
			</tr>

			</table>

						<div class="section-title" style="padding-top: 12px;"><span class="icon icon-edit"></span> AI Generation</div>
			<small style="display: block; padding-bottom: 4px;">Fine-tunes how the AI produces text. All optional. Deal analysis is a heavier one-off request, so it can use a stronger model than everyday chat; chat, routing and summaries always run at a low fixed setting.</small>

			<table id="botsCreate" style="margin-top: 5px;" cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0>

			<tr>
				<td>
					<label for="ai_analysis_model">Deal Analysis Model:
						<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
							Optional. A stronger, tool-free reasoning model used for analytical write-ups rather than live chat: one-off deal analysis, the deep-analysis final report, and the expert-analysis tool. The tool-driven research (Deep research/explore) still runs on your chat model, which is the one that must support tool calling. Must be a model your active provider offers. Leave blank to use the default chat model.
						</span></span>
					</label>
				</td>
				<td style="width: 325px;">
					<input type="text" id="ai_analysis_model" name="ai_analysis_model" class="form-field" placeholder="model name" autocomplete="off" style="width:200px; margin-top:6px;" value="<%= (((services['ai']||{})['generation'])||{}) ['analysis_model'] || '' %>">
				</td>
			</tr>

			<tr>
				<td>
					<label for="ai_chat_temperature">Chat Temperature:
						<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
							Optional. 0 = focused and consistent, higher = more varied. Applies to chat only; deal analysis and routing always run at a low fixed setting. Leave blank for the provider default.
						</span></span>
					</label>
				</td>
				<td style="width: 325px;">
					<input type="number" id="ai_chat_temperature" name="ai_chat_temperature" class="form-field" min="0" max="2" step="0.1" placeholder="(default)" style="width:100px;" value="<%= (((services['ai']||{})['generation'])||{}) ['chat_temperature'] === 0 ? '0' : ((((services['ai']||{})['generation'])||{})['chat_temperature'] || '') %>">
				</td>
			</tr>

			<tr>
				<td>
					<label for="ai_max_tokens">Max Response Tokens:
						<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
							Optional. Caps the length of chat and deal-analysis replies. Leave blank for the provider default.
						</span></span>
					</label>
				</td>
				<td style="width: 325px;">
					<input type="number" id="ai_max_tokens" name="ai_max_tokens" class="form-field" min="1" step="128" placeholder="(default)" style="width:100px;" value="<%= (((services['ai']||{})['generation'])||{}) ['max_tokens'] || '' %>">
				</td>
			</tr>

				<tr>
					<td>
						<label for="ai_num_ctx">Context Window:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								Optional (Ollama). The model's context window in tokens (num_ctx). Leave blank to use the provider default. A larger window lets the AI hold more log/deal data at once but uses more memory &mdash; set it to what your machine can run. Whatever the value, the AI protects its own instructions from being pushed out of context, so answers stay grounded.
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>
					<td style="width: 325px;">
						<input type="number" id="ai_num_ctx" name="ai_num_ctx" class="form-field" min="512" step="512" placeholder="(default)" style="width:100px;" value="<%= (((services['ai']||{})['generation'])||{}) ['num_ctx'] || '' %>">
					</td>
				</tr>

			</table>

			</div>

			<div id="aiSchedBox" class="card">

				<div class="section-title"><span class="icon icon-calendar"></span> Scheduled AI Tasks</div>
				<div style="padding: 6px 0;"><a href="./schedules" style="color: var(--link-color);">Scheduled AI Tasks now have their own <b>Schedules</b> section &mdash; open it &rarr;</a></div>

			</div>

			<div id="scheduleBox" class="card">

				<b><span class="icon icon-save"></span> System Backups</b>
				<table id="botsCreate" style="margin-top: 5px;" cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0>

				<tr>
					<td style="vertical-align: top;">
						<label for="backups">Select Days:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								These are the days to schedule system backups
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>

					<td style="width: 325px;">

						<div id="backup_days" style="display: block; width: 50px;">
							<label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
								<input type="checkbox" class="form-field" value="0"> Sunday
							</label>
							<label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
								<input type="checkbox" class="form-field" value="1"> Monday
							</label>
							<label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
								<input type="checkbox" class="form-field" value="2"> Tuesday
							</label>
							<label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
								<input type="checkbox" class="form-field" value="3"> Wednesday
							</label>
							<label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
								<input type="checkbox" class="form-field" value="4"> Thursday
							</label>
							<label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
								<input type="checkbox" class="form-field" value="5"> Friday
							</label>
							<label style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
								<input type="checkbox" class="form-field" value="6"> Saturday
							</label>
						</div>
					</td>
				</tr>

				<tr>
					<td>
						<label for="backups">Time:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								This is the time to schedule system backups
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>

					<td style="width: 325px;">
						<input type="text" id="backup_time" style="width: 60px;" class="form-field" placeholder="HH:MM">
						<span id="backup_tz_label" style="margin-left: 8px; opacity: 0.75; font-size: var(--fs-body);"></span>
					</td>
				</tr>

				<tr>
					<td>
						<label for="backup_dst">Fixed local time:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								Off (default): the backup time is stored in UTC, so it shows correctly for anyone in any timezone but shifts by an hour across daylight-saving changes. On: the backup is pinned to <b>your</b> local time and stays fixed year-round.
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>
					<td style="width: 325px;">
						<label style="cursor: pointer;"><input type="checkbox" id="backup_dst" style="width: auto; margin-right: 5px; vertical-align: middle;"> Keep fixed to my local time across DST</label>
					</td>
				</tr>

				<tr>
					<td>
						<label for="backups">Day of Month:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								This is the day of the month to schedule system backups
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>

					<td style="width: 325px;">
						<input type="number" id="backup_day_month" min="1" max="31" class="form-field" placeholder="1-31"> (Optional)
					</td>
				</tr>

				<tr>
					<td>
						<label for="backups">Maximum Backups:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								This is the maximum number of backups to keep
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>

					<td style="width: 325px;">
						<input type="number" id="backup_max" class="form-field" placeholder="">
					</td>
				</tr>

				<tr>
					<td>
						<label for="backups">Encryption Password:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								This is the password that will be used to encrypt the system backup archives
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>

					<td style="width: 325px;">
						<input type="password" autocomplete="off" id="backup_password" class="form-field" style="width: 200px;" placeholder="">
						<span id="showPassword" style="margin-left: 10px; cursor: pointer; color: var(--link-color);">Show</span>
						<% if (services['cron_backup'] && services['cron_backup']['password_set']) { %>
							<div style="margin-top: 4px; font-size: var(--fs-body); color: var(--green-color, var(--color-success));">&#10003; Password is set &mdash; leave blank to keep it</div>
						<% } %>
					</td>
				</tr>

				<tr>
					<td>
						<label for="backup_include_chats">Include AI Chats:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								When enabled, AI chat conversations are included in scheduled automatic backups
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>
					<td style="width: 325px;">
						<input type="checkbox" id="toggleBackupIncludeChats" name="backup_include_chats" class="form-field">
					</td>
				</tr>

				<tr>
					<td>
						<label for="backup_include_schedules">Include Schedules:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								When enabled, scheduled jobs (including this backup's settings and any stored SFTP credentials) are included in backups. Disable to keep credentials out of backup archives.
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>
					<td style="width: 325px;">
						<input type="checkbox" id="toggleBackupIncludeSchedules" name="backup_include_schedules" class="form-field" checked>
					</td>
				</tr>

				<tr>
					<td>
						<label for="backup_include_config">Include Configuration:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								When enabled, scheduled backups also bundle your configuration (app settings + exchange keys + Hub config), making each backup a complete, portable recovery unit. Off by default: the archive then carries your exchange keys, and this also uploads them to any off-site (SFTP) destination, so only enable it if that is what you want. A configuration-bearing backup only opens on a server using the same app password.
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>
					<td style="width: 325px;">
						<input type="checkbox" id="toggleBackupIncludeConfig" name="backup_include_config" class="form-field">
					</td>
				</tr>

				<tr>
					<td>Enabled:</td>

					<td>
						<input id="toggleBackup" name="backup_enabled" type=checkbox>
					</td>
				</tr>
				</table>
			</div>

			<div class="card">

				<b><span class="icon icon-key"></span> SFTP Credentials For Backups</b>
				<table id="botsCreate" style="margin-top: 5px;" cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0>

				<tr>
					<td>
						<label for="backups">Host:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								This is the SFTP host to upload backups
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>

					<td>
						<input name="sftp_host" id="sftp_host" class="form-field" style="width: 250px;" value="<%= services['cron_backup']['sftp']['host'] %>">
					</td>
				</tr>

				<tr>
					<td>
						<label for="backups">Port:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								This is the SFTP port
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>

					<td>
						<input name="sftp_port" id="sftp_port" class="form-field" style="width: 50px;" value="<%= services['cron_backup']['sftp']['port'] %>">
					</td>
				</tr>

				<tr>
					<td>
						<label for="backups">Username:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								This is the SFTP username
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>

					<td>
						<input name="sftp_username" id="sftp_username" class="form-field" style="width: 250px;" value="<%= services['cron_backup']['sftp']['username'] %>">
					</td>
				</tr>

				<tr>
					<td>
						<label for="backups">Password:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								This is the SFTP password
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>

					<td>
						<input type="password" autocomplete="off" name="sftp_password" id="sftp_password" class="form-field secretClearField" style="width: 250px;" value="" placeholder="<%= (services['cron_backup'] && services['cron_backup']['sftp'] && services['cron_backup']['sftp']['password_set']) ? 'Leave blank to keep the saved password' : '' %>">
						<span id="showSftpPassword" style="margin-left: 10px; cursor: pointer; color: var(--link-color);">Show</span>
						<%- include('partialsSecretClear', { field: 'sftp_password', isSet: (services['cron_backup'] && services['cron_backup']['sftp'] && services['cron_backup']['sftp']['password_set']), label: 'Password is set' }) %>
					</td>
				</tr>

				<tr>
					<td style="vertical-align: top; padding-top: 6px;">
						<label for="sftp_private_key">Private Key:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								Paste the contents of your private key file (e.g. id_rsa or id_ed25519). The key will be encrypted and stored securely. Leave blank to keep the existing key.
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>

					<td>
						<input type="hidden" name="sftp_private_key_clear" id="sftp_private_key_clear" value="0">
						<textarea name="sftp_private_key" id="sftp_private_key" class="form-field" style="width: 350px; height: 120px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--fs-label); resize: vertical;" placeholder="Paste private key here (leave blank to keep existing)"></textarea>
						<% if (services['cron_backup']['sftp']['private_key_set']) { %>
							<div id="sftp_private_key_status" style="margin-top: 4px; font-size: var(--fs-body); color: var(--green-color, var(--color-success));">&#10003; Private key is set &nbsp;<span id="sftp_clear_key" style="cursor: pointer; color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--fs-body);">[Clear]</span></div>
						<% } else { %>
							<div id="sftp_private_key_status" style="margin-top: 4px; font-size: var(--fs-body); display: none;"></div>
						<% } %>
					</td>
				</tr>

				<tr>
					<td>
						<label for="backups">Passphrase:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								This an optional passphrase for your private key
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>

					<td>
						<input type="password" autocomplete="off" name="sftp_passphrase" id="sftp_passphrase" class="form-field secretClearField" style="width: 250px;" value="" placeholder="<%= (services['cron_backup'] && services['cron_backup']['sftp'] && services['cron_backup']['sftp']['passphrase_set']) ? 'Leave blank to keep the saved passphrase' : '' %>">
						<span id="showSftpPassphrase" style="margin-left: 10px; cursor: pointer; color: var(--link-color);">Show</span>
						<%- include('partialsSecretClear', { field: 'sftp_passphrase', isSet: (services['cron_backup'] && services['cron_backup']['sftp'] && services['cron_backup']['sftp']['passphrase_set']), label: 'Passphrase is set' }) %>
					</td>
				</tr>

				<tr>
					<td>
						<label for="backups">Upload Directory:
							<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
								This is the path on the remote host where your backups will be uploaded.
								<br><br>
								NOTE: This should be a unique and empty directory as files will be automatically removed according to the value set for maximum backups
							</span></span>
						</label>
					</td>

					<td>
						<input name="sftp_remote_directory" id="sftp_remote_directory" class="form-field" style="width: 250px;" value="<%= services['cron_backup']['sftp']['remote_directory'] %>">
					</td>
				</tr>

				<tr>
					<td>Enabled:</td>

					<td>
						<input id="toggleSftp" name="sftp_enabled" type=checkbox>
					</td>
				</tr>
				</table>
			</div>


			<div class="card">

				<% var mailerCfg = services['mailer'] || {}; %>
				<%- include('./partialsMailerSettings', {
					mailer: {
						enabled: !!mailerCfg.enabled, host: mailerCfg.host || '', port: mailerCfg.port || 587,
						secure: !!mailerCfg.secure, user: mailerCfg.user || '', from: mailerCfg.from || '',
						password_set: !!mailerCfg.password
					},
					hubOverride: true
				}) %>
			</div>

			<div class="card">

				<div class="section-title"><span class="icon icon-stop"></span> Circuit Breaker</div>
				<table id="botsCreate" style="margin-top: 5px;" cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0>

					<tr>
						<td>
							<label for="cb_deal_ratio_threshold">Deal Ratio:
								<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
									Fraction of active deals that must trigger safety orders within the window to activate (e.g. 0.5 = 50%)
								</span></span>
							</label>
						</td>

						<td style="width: 325px;">
							<input type="number" id="cb_deal_ratio_threshold" name="cb_deal_ratio_threshold" class="form-field" step="0.1" min="0.1" max="1.0" style="width:80px;">
						</td>
					</tr>

					<tr>
						<td>
							<label for="cb_deal_ratio_window_secs">Deal Ratio Window:
								<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
									Rolling time window in seconds for counting simultaneous safety order triggers
								</span></span>
							</label>
						</td>

						<td style="width: 325px;">
							<input type="number" id="cb_deal_ratio_window_secs" name="cb_deal_ratio_window_secs" class="form-field" min="5" max="300" style="width:80px;">
						</td>
					</tr>

					<tr>
						<td>
							<label for="cb_price_drop_percent">Price Drop %:
								<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
									Percentage price drop within the window that triggers the circuit breaker for that pair
								</span></span>
							</label>
						</td>

						<td style="width: 325px;">
							<input type="number" id="cb_price_drop_percent" name="cb_price_drop_percent" class="form-field" step="0.5" min="1" max="50" style="width:80px;">
						</td>
					</tr>

					<tr>
						<td>
							<label for="cb_price_drop_window_secs">Price Drop Window:
								<span class="toolTip">?<span class="toolTipText">
									Rolling time window in seconds for measuring price drops
								</span></span>
							</label>
						</td>

						<td style="width: 325px;">
							<input type="number" id="cb_price_drop_window_secs" name="cb_price_drop_window_secs" class="form-field" min="10" max="600" style="width:80px;">
						</td>
					</tr>

					<tr>
						<td>
							<label for="togglePriceDrop">Price Drop Trigger:
